    {
      "id": "claim_d1c06841e2654e119391dffece76f243",
      "statement": "AGENT DECK runs as three cooperating processes: an outer supervisor (`electron .`, the default entry) that takes the machine's single-instance lock, hides explorer's native desktop icons, spawns a detached restore watcher and the panel child, and restores the icons when that child exits; the panel main process (`electron . --panel`, the cordis kernel) that owns the window, 25 ms cursor-polled hotzones, z-order pinning, tray, bridge IPC, search, settings, session-row focus and the desktop-component plugin host; and an Electron `utilityProcess` child (`dist/main/dataplane.js`) that runs all four collection services (sessions, hardware, usage log, desktop carry) together with their timers and pushes one snapshot per second back to the panel.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/dataplane.ts#L1-L59",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:153db68377e6420f58e047db5ad321d377aab060255b04a6e250f5f3a5646397:"
