    {
      "id": "claim_d98a59121e9f4173b7fbf1c7fa629e77",
      "statement": "Runtime mode is decided solely by `process.argv`: with no flag the process is the outer supervisor, `--panel` runs the panel process which holds the single-instance lock for its whole life (a second launch is refused with a `single-instance-refused` event while the running instance receives `second-instance` and re-shows the panel), `--accept` runs the acceptance battery with both lock branches bypassed, and `--icon-restore` forces the native desktop icons visible and exits without taking the lock.",
      "evidence": [
